+## 12. Record, file and directory formats
+
+All integers are little-endian. Hex in text files is lowercase.
+
+### 12.1 Canonical state S_u (264 bytes)
+
+| Off | Bytes | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 128 | genotypes[32], u32 |
+| 128 | 128 | caches[32], u32; 0 where invalid |
+| 256 | 4 | policy_mask (bit i = 1 iff slot i is M) |
+| 260 | 4 | cache_valid_mask |
+
+### 12.2 History digest chain
+
+- `D_0` = SHA-256 of the ASCII string `BRC2-HIST-V2` (12 bytes), then u32 block_id, then S_0.
+- For u = 1..t−1, `D_u` = SHA-256 of a 306-byte message:
+  - `D_(u−1)` (32 bytes);
+  - u16 u;
+  - u32 T_u;
+  - u32 retries_u (total survival rejections at update u);
+  - S_u.
+- The record stores `D_(t−1)`.
+
+### 12.3 Block record (2,088 bytes)
+
+**Header (offsets 0–103)**
+
+| Off | Bytes | Type | Field and constraint |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 4 | ASCII | `BRC2` |
+| 4 | 2 | u16 | layout_version = 2 |
+| 6 | 2 | u16 | record_length = 2088 |
+| 8 | 4 | u32 | block_id |
+| 12 | 1 | u8 | start_code = block_id & 1 (0 = ALL_F) |
+| 13 | 1 | u8 | R_t |
+| 14 | 2 | u16 | checkpoint t (as used; 256 in benchmark-r1) |
+| 16 | 4 | u32 | CHECKPOINT_TIME word0, the actual Philox value |
+| 20 | 4 | u32 | T_(t−2) |
+| 24 | 4 | u32 | T_(t−1) |
+| 28 | 4 | u32 | I_t |
+| 32 | 4 | u32 | T_t |
+| 36 | 4 | u32 | eligible_mask E |
+| 40 | 1 | u8 | e |
+| 41 | 1 | u8 | H |
+| 42 | 1 | u8 | focal_slot (0xFF if H = 0) |
+| 43 | 1 | u8 | factual_target_code = 1 − R_t |
+| 44 | 8 | u64 | focal_key = κ_f* if H = 1; 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF if H = 0 |
+| 52 | 4 | u32 | pre-target policy_mask |
+| 56 | 4 | u32 | pre-target cache_valid_mask |
+| 60 | 4 | u32 | history_queries = 128(t−1) |
+| 64 | 4 | u32 | checkpoint_queries = 768 |
+| 68 | 4 | u32 | history_survival_retries |
+| 72 | 32 | bytes | history_digest D_(t−1) |
+
+**State and arm sections**
+
+| Off | Bytes | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 104 | 128 | pre-target genotypes[32] |
+| 232 | 128 | pre-target caches[32] (0 where invalid) |
+| 360 | 1680 | arms 0..5; arm a at 360 + 280a |
+
+**Arm section (280 bytes)**
+
+The section has two parts.
+
+- **Arm metadata, bytes [0, 8):** validated against §4.3; never part of payload equality.
+- **Scientific payload, bytes [8, 280):** compared for equality.
+
+| Off | Bytes | Field | Part |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 1 | u8 arm_code a | metadata |
+| 1 | 1 | u8 target_code | metadata |
+| 2 | 1 | u8 retrieval_code | metadata |
+| 3 | 1 | u8 is_factual | metadata |
+| 4 | 4 | u32 switched_mask Q | metadata |
+| 8 | 2 | u16 queries = 128 | payload |
+| 10 | 2 | u16 survival_retries | payload |
+| 12 | 1 | u8 D_E | payload |
+| 13 | 1 | u8 d_f | payload |
+| 14 | 2 | u16 A | payload |
+| 16 | 4 | u32 post_policy_mask | payload |
+| 20 | 4 | u32 candidate_mismatch_sum (0..4096) | payload |
+| 24 | 256 | survivors[32] × 8 bytes, slot order | payload |
+
+**Survivor entry (8 bytes)**
+
+| Off | Bytes | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 1 | u8 j |
+| 1 | 1 | u8 m |
+| 2 | 1 | u8 post_policy |
+| 3 | 1 | u8 draw_retries |
+| 4 | 4 | u32 genotype |
+
+**Payload equality.** "Arms a and a′ are payload-equal" means record bytes [360+280a+8, 360+280a+280) equal bytes [360+280a′+8, 360+280a′+280).
+
+**Numerator and integrity section**
+
+| Off | Bytes | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 2040 | 1 | i8 NL_rec |
+| 2041 | 1 | i8 NL_inn |
+| 2042 | 2 | i16 NP_rec |
+| 2044 | 2 | i16 NP_inn |
+| 2046 | 1 | i8 NF_rec |
+| 2047 | 1 | i8 NF_inn |
+| 2048 | 4 | u32 total_queries = 128(t+5) |
+| 2052 | 4 | u32 block_status = 0 |
+| 2056 | 32 | SHA-256 of record bytes [0, 2056) |
+
+### 12.4 Chunk files
+
+**Layout.**
+
+- Files are `chunk_KK.bin`, with KK a two-digit decimal from 00 to k−1.
+- Chunk K holds blocks 1000K up to min(1000K+999, n−1), ascending.
+
+**Chunk header (64 bytes)**
+
+| Off | Bytes | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 8 | ASCII `BRC2CHNK` |
+| 8 | 2 | u16 layout_version = 2 |
+| 10 | 2 | u16 chunk_index |
+| 12 | 4 | u32 first_block |
+| 16 | 4 | u32 block_count |
+| 20 | 4 | u32 record_length = 2088 |
+| 24 | 4 | u32 tier_code |
+| 28 | 4 | u32 reserved = 0 |
+| 32 | 32 | producer build ID (raw) |
+
+**Chunk sizes.**
+
+| Tier | Chunk sizes | All chunk bytes |
+|---|---|---|
+| production-r1 | 42 × 2,088,064 | 87,698,688 |
+| benchmark-r1 | 2,088,064 + 50,176 | 2,138,240 |
+| fixture-r1 | 33,472 | 33,472 |
+
+### 12.5 Trace file `trace_audit_blocks.bin`
+
+**Header (32 bytes):**
+
+- ASCII `BRC2TRCE`;
+- u16 version = 2;
+- u16 n_blocks (from the tier table);
+- u32 tier_code;
+- 16 zero bytes.
+
+**Body.** For each trace block in ascending order: u32 block_id, u16 t, u16 n = t, then n × 32 bytes holding D_0..D_(t−1).
+
+**Size** = 32 + Σ(8 + 32t_b).
+
+| Tier | Trace size |
+|---|---|
+| production-r1 | 395,808 to 524,832 bytes |
+| benchmark-r1 | exactly 524,832 bytes |
+| fixture-r1 | 98,976 to 131,232 bytes |
+
+Readers compute the exact expected size.
+
+### 12.6 Manifest
+
+`MANIFEST.txt` is ASCII with LF endings and no trailing spaces, ending with exactly one LF. Its lines, in order:
+
+```
+BRC2-MANIFEST-V2
+study=PHASE3-BIT-RETRIEVAL-CAUSALITY-002
+protocol_sha256=<64 lowercase hex: SHA-256 of this v0.4 file>
+tier=<production-r1|benchmark-r1|fixture-r1>
+producer_build_id=<64 lowercase hex>
+blocks=<n>
+chunk_blocks=1000
+chunks=<k>
+record_length=2088
+file chunk_00.bin <bytes> <64 lowercase hex>
+...                         (one line per chunk, ascending)
+file trace_audit_blocks.bin <bytes> <64 lowercase hex>
+total_queries=<decimal>
+complete=1
+```
+
+**Number format.** Decimals have no sign and no leading zeros (zero is `0`).
+
+**MANIFEST.sha256** contains exactly `<64 lowercase hex>␠␠MANIFEST.txt\n`, the `sha256sum` format.
+
+### 12.7 Run directory layout
+
+For run root `<RUN>`, the paths are:
+
+| Path | Writer | Contents |
+|---|---|---|
+| `<RUN>/data/` | producer only | Data inventory (§13.1) |
+| `<RUN>/results/RESULTS_ANALYZER.txt` | analyzer | Results |
+| `<RUN>/audit/RESULTS_AUDITOR.txt`, `<RUN>/audit/AUDIT_REPORT.txt` | auditor | Results and audit report |
+| `<RUN>/agreement/AGREEMENT.txt` | job script | Agreement record |
+| `<RUN>/logs/` | job script | stdout, stderr, per-step timing and exit codes |
+
+**Rules.**
+
+- The producer refuses to start (exit 2) unless `<RUN>/data/` is absent or empty.
+- During writing, temporary files are named `.tmp.<final name>` inside `data/`.
+- Results files are written with mode 0400.
+
+### 12.8 Output budget
+
+**Production.**
+
+| Item | Size |
+|---|---|
+| Chunks | 87,698,688 bytes |
+| Trace | ≤ 524,832 bytes |
+| Manifests | < 8 KiB |
+| Results, report and agreement | < 1 MiB |
+| Logs (capped by the job script) | ≤ 16 MiB |
+| **Total** | **< 110 MB** |
+
+The total is within the 1 GiB readiness limit and the 2 GiB hard cap. The producer refuses to write beyond 1 GiB.
