+All three paths absolute and strict as above. This tool is fixture-only, never
+called by scientific CLI as a parameter override. Parsed public cases have an
+externally fixed result even if that result is ERROR; the tool writes canonical
+FIXOUT JSON and exits with INDEX.json's expected_exit. Such expected error
+FIXOUT is an engineering artifact, never a VALID science result. Invalid outer
+case syntax, unknown case kind, unauthenticated files or output collision returns
+exit2 with BRS3_ERROR INPUT/FORMAT/CLI and no FIXOUT. Internal failures exit5.
+For well-formed cases testing an error, output schema is fixed by FIXTURE_SPEC;
+stderr first line is BRS3_ERROR <case error code>, even if code is fixture-only.
+Public fixture execution reads ONLY authenticated FIXTURE_VIEW bytes under
+9.1.1, NEVER expectedpath/expected output bytes. INDEX supplies input membership,
+not an output lookup. Expected files remain solely on the ROOT coordinator;
+full authentication precedes expected-free FRCE staging and byte comparison
+follows actual computed output retrieval. The executable validates its projected
+view rather than reopening the full bundle to authenticate absent answers.
+Own --self-test cannot satisfy this public-input comparison. No literal full
+fixture-r1 RNG/history answers are asserted here; each independent author must
+compute all 16 full trajectories only on FRCE after SOURCEGO, freeze own FIXOUT
+and binaries before cross-access, then compare after G4a. POST_G4_REQUIREMENTS.json
+fixes these later tests and their failure meaning; it is not a controller or
+assertion that they have passed. All a-k public primitives and manual cases have
+literal answers; random full-trajectory and corruption outcomes require execution.
+
+9.4 Inference/presentation
+The 11 canonical result lines in section 5 are exhaustive and contain no rounded
+statistics. For production define e_M=policy_signed_sum/163840000 and
+e_A=accuracy_signed_sum/5242880000. Use h_M=19778834661/1000000000000 and
+h_A=23018074131/1000000000000, clip e+-h to [-1,1], then apply G0's ordered
+strict/non-strict predicates exactly. Never classify rounded endpoints. Reduced
+rationals use num/den with positive denominator, gcd1, canonical signed numerator.
+Separate post-acceptance presentation: mean is exact reduced fraction; interval
+is exact reduced fraction pair; displayed lower floor(10^12*lower)/10^12 and
+upper ceil(10^12*upper)/10^12, printed fixed12 decimals (no negative zero).
+No recomputed halfwidth for fixture or benchmark. Certificate uses n=48 terms
+k=0..47, tail starts exponent97 and denominator97; both grid ceilings proven.
+Family alpha is 1/25+1/100=1/20. No old L/F classification or key imports.
+
+9.5 Runtime completion requirements
+Parallel producer AND independent full auditor must support --threads 1..32;
+full blocks can be scheduled independently and emitted in ascending order with
+bounded streaming. No entire 4.16GB data RAM requirement, no reduced audit.
+The one whole-workflow 64-block benchmark includes producer, analyzer, FULL
+independent audit, comparison, IO, hashing, accounting and sealing. Its actual
+whole elapsed must be <=23.04 seconds since 2*(20000/64)*23.04=14400 seconds.
+The G0 memory, 16GiB output, 8h original-allocation and all-step constraints
+remain binding. A failed benchmark stops the design, not another tuning trial.
+No benchmark endpoints displayed. Source and fixture expectations may be reviewed
+here, but all scientific builds/fixtures/RNG execution are FRCE Slurm only.
