+PHASE3-BIT-SUSTAINED-RETRIEVAL-003 — prospective protocol v0.1
+25 October 2026. DRAFT FOR INDEPENDENT SCIENTIFIC REVIEW; NOT EXECUTION AUTHORITY.
+
+1. Question, authority and boundaries
+Does sustained availability of cached proposals, rather than fresh substitutions,
+change subsequent memory-policy enrichment in the supplied BIT/PL model?
+Human authority: USER_AUTHORITY.json. This is separate new work, not a rerun,
+extension, top-up, pooled analysis or replacement of BIT002 or Studies001–003.
+The original incomplete broader Phase3 remains incomplete. Published v1.3.0
+and all earlier evidence remain immutable. No scientific job is authorized by
+this candidate. No parameter sweep or revival of the original large protocol.
+
+The intervention identifies a total downstream effect of a specified sustained
+proposal rule, including state, competition and policy-frequency feedback. It
+does not identify natural mediation, a fraction of earlier enrichment mediated
+by retrieval, evolution of a new memory architecture, retention versus retrieval
+selection, per-carrier fitness, invasion or equilibrium. No biological inference,
+recurrence-law intervention or cross-operator generality follows. "Enrichment"
+here means policy frequency over a fixed follow-up under continuing mutation,
+not a pure selection coefficient or absence of mutation effects.
+
+2. Binding model reference and exact intervention
+Normative reference is BIT002 PROTOCOL_V0_4_ACCEPTED.txt SHA256
+71ccc1d065fa4868c30f96588ec34312bdc435e1047214c60b1f5643846c7daa,
+sections2.1–2.4 ONLY for state, initialization, HALF target law and full turnover;
+section5.1 for Philox4x32-10 algorithm; section12.1 for state serialization.
+A byte-identical copy must accompany this candidate and every implementation.
+Other BIT002 checkpoints, keys, endpoints, inference, submission counts and
+resource rules are NOT imported. The present document explicitly overrides
+update ranges, key strings, initialization mixture and switched-set scheduling.
+
+32slots, uint32 genotypes/caches, policies F/M. Exactly four candidates/parent:
+parent; cached-or-fresh policy probe; global scout; donor-mutated local child.
+128evaluations/turnover. Integer Plackett–Luce without replacement32survivors,
+the reference tie rules, local/policy mutations1/32 and survivor cache transition
+apply unchanged. Reference survival rejection index256 invalidates the run.
+An M survivor retains its producing parent's pre-update genotype as its cache;
+an F survivor has invalid zero cache. This applies in BOTH branches even when
+retrieval is disabled. No cache deletion, altered mutation, clamped policy,
+extra proposal, extra query or change in retention/inheritance is permitted.
+
+Each block starts at update0 with random genotypes and invalid caches; even
+block IDs ALL_F, odd ALL_M. Generate a common factual CACHE history updates
+1..256 using Q=empty. Checkpoint is the complete post-update256 state S256;
+it is fixed in advance, not selected for frequency, eligibility or performance.
+Copy S256 exactly into branches C and A. Follow both through updates257..512:
+ C: Q=empty at every update, cached probes available under reference eligibility.
+ A: Q={i: pol_i=M and v_i=1 in THAT BRANCH'S current pre-update state}.
+Thus A always substitutes the already-defined fresh policy probe at its current
+eligible slots; C and A recompute eligibility independently after diverging.
+Both branches feed their OWN survivors, genotypes, policies and caches into the
+next turnover. No shadow is discarded after a single step. No forcing states,
+lineages or eligibility to remain matched. Both face the SAME target T_u at
+each absolute update, including recurrence across the checkpoint boundary.
+
+The intervention deliberately changes cached information to a fresh search
+proposal, and through donor choice may also change the local child. Equal
+candidate/query budgets do not establish equal informational value or a pure
+retrieval operation stripped of its search opportunity tradeoff. No separate
+storage/energy charge is invented. Report this composite proposal contrast.
+
+3. Population, independence and random-number coupling
+Production: exactly20,000new independent blocks b=0..19999;10,000ALL_F and
+10,000ALL_M. Unit is a full paired block. Survivors, generations, two branches
+and the two start groups are not independent replicates. Estimand is the equal
+mixture of the two initial-start distributions; no favorable subgroup selection.
+
+Use reference Philox and extraction, with exactly9purposes:
+INITIAL_GENOTYPE, TARGET_INNOVATION, TARGET_COPY, FRESH_MASK, SCOUT_MASK,
+LOCAL_BIT, DONOR_KEY, SURVIVAL_UNIFORM, POLICY_MUTATION.
+For tier tau in {production-r1,fixture-r1,benchmark-r1}, key input is literal
+ASCII PHASE3-BIT-SUSTAINED-RETRIEVAL-003|<tau>|<PURPOSE>, no terminator.
+SHA256 digest bytes0..3 and4..7 are little-endian k0,k1. Counter=(b,u,entity,
+subindex), and extraction/entity/subindex semantics are reference5.3 restricted
+to these9purposes. INITIAL_GENOTYPE only u=0,slot0..31. Other purposes use
+u=1..512. FOCAL_PARENT and CHECKPOINT_TIME do not exist in this study.
+Targets: innovations from word0, copy from word0&1; T1=I1,T2=I2 and foru>=3
+T_u=T_(u-2) if copybit1, else I_u. Candidate identities, masks, donor keys,
+mutation slots and survival draw/retry addresses match the reference.
+
+All target innovations/copy bits through512 are common to history and branches.
+All six turnover-purpose arrays are shared between C and A at the same
+(b,u,slot/bit/draw/retry), NEVER keyed by arm, policy, realized score or worker.
+These six are FRESH_MASK,SCOUT_MASK,LOCAL_BIT,DONOR_KEY,SURVIVAL_UNIFORM,
+POLICY_MUTATION; INITIAL is separate, giving9total with the two target purposes.
+No extra RNG purpose is allowed.
+Each draw starts retry0 even if another arm consumed more retries. Arm order
+and thread scheduling never change addresses. Coupling reduces noise but does
+not keep evolved states or families identical. Each branch has its intended
+marginal law under the independent-uniform-address working idealization.
+Distinct purpose key pairs must be independently computed twice, pairwise
+distinct across27newkeys and disjoint from all previously registered project
+purpose keys, including BIT002. Freeze authenticated complete registry/G1F
+before compilation. No generation to search for keys with favorable outcomes.
+Philox is deterministic; distinct addresses do not prove independence. The
+following inferential coverage is conditional on that working idealization.
+
+4. Exactly one primary and one secondary endpoint
+Let m_bzu = number of M policies in post-update state for armz at updateu.
+Let a_bzu = sum over its32post-update survivor genotypes of
+(32-popcount(genotype XOR T_u)); range0..1024. These are realized surviving
+population accuracy scores, not all-candidate scores and not ancestral scores.
+For z in {C,A}, define integer sums over u=257..512:
+ M_bz=sum m_bzu, range0..8192;
+ A_bz=sum a_bzu, range0..262144.
+Primary block contrast X_b=(M_bC-M_bA)/8192 in[-1,1].
+Secondary block contrast Y_b=(A_bC-A_bA)/262144 in[-1,1].
+Primary theta_M=(E_ALL_F X+E_ALL_M X)/2; secondary theta_A analogously.
+Both estimates are arithmetic means of all20,000block contrasts, computed
+from exact signed integer totals. No conditioning on caches, H/e, final policy,
+survival, recurrence events or response. Zero contrasts remain in the cohort.
+No further confirmatory endpoints, time-window search, terminal-frequency test,
+per-carrier ratio, post hoc subgroup, mediation decomposition or effect curve.
+Checkpoint start-group counts and validity/accounting checks are descriptive
+engineering evidence only; not extra scientific hypothesis tests.
+
+5. Inference and fixed decision rules
+Two simultaneous two-sided Hoeffding intervals, no outcome-based variance fit:
+alpha_M=.04, alpha_A=.01, family sum=.05. For independent, not necessarily
+identically distributed, paired block contrasts with range length2,
+h=sqrt(2*ln(2/alpha)/20000). Fixed outward conservative rational halfwidths:
+h_M=19778834661/10^12=.019778834661;
+h_A=23018074131/10^12=.023018074131.
+Independent G1F arithmetic must certify each rational >= its mathematical
+halfwidth using a directed interval calculation, not agreement of two floats.
+Intervals are [max(-1,estimate-h),min(1,estimate+h)]. Exact rational arithmetic
+controls classification; decimal endpoints are rounded outward for presentation.
+Coverage is joint at least95% conditional on the RNG idealization, for these
+two new endpoints only, not all past/future manuscripts. Mean and interval are
+reported for BOTH even if primary is adverse, bounded or unresolved.
+
+For BOTH endpoints, meaningful threshold delta=1/32=.03125 and equivalence
+margin epsilon=1/32, in the normalized endpoint's own units. Classification:
+ MATERIAL_POSITIVE iff lower>delta; MATERIAL_NEGATIVE iff upper<-delta;
+ BOUNDED_WITHIN_MARGIN iff lower>=-epsilon and upper<=epsilon;
+ POSITIVE_MAGNITUDE_UNRESOLVED iff lower>0 otherwise;
+ NEGATIVE_MAGNITUDE_UNRESOLVED iff upper<0 otherwise;
+ UNRESOLVED otherwise. Apply this order. Equality atdelta is not material.
+For theta_M these are3.125percentage points of time-averaged policy frequency;
+for theta_A3.125percentage points of normalized survivor accuracy (one bit).
+Within-margin does not mean exact zero or absence. Negative estimates, bounds,
+all intervals and unresolved classifications must remain visible. No increase
+in N, revised margin, extra horizon, optional stopping or new seed after results.
+This is guaranteed precision under an assumption, not guaranteed power or a
+promise of significance. At zero, fixed intervals fit the chosen margin.
+
+6. Tiers and query/work counts
+Fixture tier: randomblocks0..15, full256history+256pairedfollow-up. Public
+constructed states/corner cases and expected public results are separately
+frozen G1F inputs; they may not use production keys or outcomes.
+Benchmark tier: blocks0..63 at the full scientific horizon;32ofeach start.
+Benchmark is timing/resource-only, not a scientific diagnostic. Numeric endpoint
+totals must not be displayed, interpreted or used to change design. No benchmark
+effect estimate is an observation supporting the paper.
+Production has20,000*(256+2*256)=15,360,000turnovers and1,966,080,000candidate
+queries by the producer. Full independent replay entails the same additional
+turnovers/query work; no assertion that this audit cost is negligible. Analyzer
+can recompute sums from stored states and targets without a third scientific
+simulation. Include analysis,audit,IO,hashing and sealing in qualification.
+
+7. Stored data and independent full-history assurance
+Every block stores its exact S0, all256historypost-states, then256Cpost-states
+and256Apost-states. States use the reference264byte little-endian layout. Store
+all512targets, selected per-update retry totals (768u32), four integer endpoint
+sums, metadata/block/start flags, and checksummed file inventories. A complete
+new record-format/CLI contract is a PREBUILD G1F deliverable, not an unreviewed
